{
  "new_prompts": {
    "F4": {
      "lead": "A printed page from a 1981 Lithuanian civil-defence training album, drawn and printed like the Soviet Grazhdanskaya Oborona wall charts of 1975-1985: a dark-brown brush-and-ink outline around every figure and object, thin matte gouache fills with one soft shadow tone, four-colour offset lithography with a faint coarse halftone, muted inks of dusty blue, olive, ochre, brick red and grey-brown on pale bright cream paper. The pale cream paper itself is the background and the sky: the main subject is drawn as a cut-out vignette directly on it, its ground fading to a soft edge, with wide empty margins; insets are small ruled boxes on the same paper. Flat even diagram lighting. People are ordinary Soviet-era Lithuanians of 1981, anonymous types: broad plain faces, heavy features, closed mouths and a level direct gaze; sturdy thick-set bodies; men's hair short, combed flat and side-parted, women's short and practical or under a cotton headscarf; cheap loosely cut state-made clothes in brown, olive, dusty blue, grey and dull red; every movement one stiff held position.",
      "suffix": "Finish: flat muted offset print on pale bright cream paper, brush-ink outlines, plain sturdy Soviet-era people, the subject floating on bare paper with wide margins.",
      "notes": "The predicted splice: F2 print-production paragraph + F3 people block, trimmed. Paper stated as PALE BRIGHT cream (all F1-F3 output came out darker/dun than 1.5). Composition stated as cut-out vignette with the paper as sky, to push Sunburst off full-bleed. Default production candidate; everything else is a one-attribute edit of it."
    },
    "F4dun": {
